0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-10-09) plus the 2026-11-20 changes:
0000                             ;        [x stores in a variable, "[ " pushes an anonymous block, any other
0000                             ;        character after [ is an error, the heap pointer lives at z10+.
0000                             ;        The string escape is "/" (it was ">").
0000                             ;        Dividing by zero is not checked. -n? does no more editing than
0000                             ;        Backspace.
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two builds, selected by the CHECKED line below (CPM is always 0: the 6809
0000                             ;  has no CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: "B8Script checks nothing")
0000                             ;             1 = stops on stack overrun, Ctrl-C, heap past the limit, a store
0000                             ;                 outside the program's own space, and a bad character after [,
0000                             ;                 printing a letter and the place, like  S @ 245
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack, 127 entries; empty = 8100h; S stays inside
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack, 127 cells; empty = 8200h; U stays inside
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF0Bh  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY) and EXIT are supplied
0000                             ;                 by the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty data stack
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Checked build: the error report. It is here, ahead of the inner loop, so
F000                             ;  that the loop's stack checks reach it with short branches.
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
                                 ; a 3-byte CMPX # (the 8Ch), so they all fall through to `error`.
                    E_STACK:   LDA   #"S"   ; data stack over or under
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_RSTACK:   LDA   #"R"   ; return stack over or under
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; heap past the limit
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_STORE:   LDA   #"W"   ; write outside the program's space
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_BRACK:   LDA   #"D"   ; bad character after [
                                 ; error: print the letter in A, " @ " and the offset in the program of the
                                 ; character just read, then end. For example: S @ 245
                    ERROR:    LDS   #RSTOP   ; the stacks may be wrecked: start clean
                              LDU   #DSTOP   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              LDA   #" "   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              LDA   #"@"   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              LDA   #" "   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              TFR   Y,D   
                              SUBD   #PROG+1   ; the character just read
                              PSHU   D   
                              JSR   pdec   ; and fall into fin
F000                          ENDIF      
F000   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F003                             ; =============================================================================
F003                             ;  Startup
F003                             ; =============================================================================
F003   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F007   CE 82 00               LDU   #DSTOP   
F00A   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F00C   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F00E   8E 83 00               LDX   #PROG   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
F011   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   
F013   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F015   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F017   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F019   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F01B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CLR   <KEYBUF   
F01B                          ENDIF      
F01B   10 8E 83 00            LDY   #PROG   
F01F                             ; =============================================================================
F01F                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F01F                             ; 
F01F                             ;    00h          end of program
F01F                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
F01F                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F01F                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F01F                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F01F                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F01F                             ; =============================================================================
F01F                NEXT:        
F01F                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
                                 ; Each stack lives in one page, and "empty" is the first address of
                                 ; the page above, so a stack is in range exactly when the address
                                 ; one below its pointer is in the page (127 entries or cells).
                              LEAX   -1,U   
                              TFR   X,D   
                              CMPA   #DSPAGE   
                              BNE   e_stack   
                              LEAX   -1,S   
                              TFR   X,D   
                              CMPA   #RSPAGE   
                              BNE   e_rstack   
F01F                          ENDIF      
F01F   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F021   27 DD                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F023   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F025   25 F8                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F027   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F029   25 22                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F02B   80 0F                  SUBA   #0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
F02D   81 0A                  CMPA   #0Ah   
F02F   25 2A                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F031   81 11                  CMPA   #11h   
F033   25 16                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
F035   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   ; A = c - 41h
F037   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F039   25 2C                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F03B   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F03D   25 0A                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F03F   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F041   25 1E                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F043   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F045   24 D8                  BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F047   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F049   80 09        P5B:      SUBA   #9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F04B   8B 05        P3A:      ADDA   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F04D                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F04D   8E F0 B0     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F050                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F050                             ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
F050                             ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
F050   E6 86                  LDB   A,X   
F052   81 14                  CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
F054   86 00                  LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
F056   49                     ROLA      
F057   AD 8B                  JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F059                          ENDIF      
F059                          IF   CHECKED   
                              ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
                              JSR   [A,X]   
F059                          ENDIF      
F059   20 C4                  BRA   next   
F05B                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F05B   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F05D   8D 22                  BSR   rdnum   
F05F   20 BE                  BRA   next   
F061                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F061   8D 10        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F063   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F065   20 B8                  BRA   next   
F067                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F067                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F067   8D 0A        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F069   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F06B   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F06D   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F06F   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F071   20 AC                  BRA   next   
F073                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F073   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F074   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F077   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F079   39                     RTS      
F07A                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F07A   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F07C   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F07E   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F080   39           AB9:      RTS      
F081                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F081                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F081                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F081   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F082   5F                     CLRB      
F083   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F085   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F087   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F089   31 21                  LEAY   1,Y   
F08B   34 02                  PSHS   A   
F08D   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F08F   58                     ASLB      
F090   49                     ROLA      
F091   58                     ASLB      
F092   49                     ROLA      
F093   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F095   58                     ASLB      
F096   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F097   EB E0                  ADDB   ,S+   
F099   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F09B   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F09D   20 E6                  BRA   rd1   
F09F                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F09F                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F09F                             ; return with the carry clear.
F09F                             ; (In the unchecked build it is here, ahead of the table, to leave room in
F09F                             ; the two ranges after it; the checked build has it next to the grave.)
F09F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F09F   8D D9        HEXC:     BSR   isdig   
F0A1   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F0A3   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F0A5   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F0A7   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F0A9   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F0AB   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F0AD   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F0AF   39           HV9:      RTS      
F0B0                          ENDIF      
F0B0                             ; =============================================================================
F0B0                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F0B0                             ; 
F0B0                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F0B0                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F0B0                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F0B0                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F0B0                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F0B0                             ;  stores a value.)
F0B0                             ; 
F0B0                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F0B0                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F0B0                             ; =============================================================================
F0B0                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0B0                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
F0B0                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
F0B0                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
F0B0                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
F0B0                PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
F0B0                NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F0B0                          ENDIF      
F0B0                PTAB:        
F0B0                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0B0   94                     FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
F0B1   21                     FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
F0B2   A4                     FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
F0B3   80                     FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
F0B4   CA                     FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
F0B5   D6                     FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
F0B6   79                     FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
F0B7   17                     FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
F0B8   39                     FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
F0B9   43                     FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
F0BA   DE                     FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
F0BB   31                     FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
F0BC   E5                     FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
F0BD   9B                     FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
F0BE   F0                     FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
F0BF   D1                     FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
F0C0   7D                     FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
F0C1   61                     FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
F0C2   6D                     FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
F0C3   5F                     FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
F0C4   C9                     FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
F0C5   C3                     FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
F0C6   88                     FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
F0C7   7B                     FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
F0C8   77                     FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
F0C9   28                     FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
F0CA   46                     FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
F0CB   55                     FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
F0CC   36                     FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
F0CD   20                     FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
F0CE   3E                     FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
F0CF   31                     FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F0D0                          ENDIF      
F0D0                          IF   CHECKED   
                              FDB   h_store   ; !
                              FDB   h_str   ; "
                              FDB   h_num   ; #
                              FDB   h_print   ; $
                              FDB   h_swap   ; %
                              FDB   h_and   ; &
                              FDB   h_emit   ; '
                              FDB   h_open   ; (
                              FDB   h_close   ; )
                              FDB   h_mul   ; *
                              FDB   h_add   ; +
                              FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
                              FDB   h_sub   ; -
                              FDB   h_cstore   ; .
                              FDB   h_div   ; /
                              FDB   h_dup   ; :
                              FDB   h_drop   ; ;
                              FDB   h_lt   ; <
                              FDB   h_eq   ; =
                              FDB   h_gt   ; >
                              FDB   h_key   ; ?
                              FDB   h_fetch   ; @
                              FDB   h_def   ; [
                              FDB   h_break   ; \
                              FDB   h_ret   ; ]
                              FDB   h_xor   ; ^
                              FDB   h_alloc   ; _
                              FDB   h_grave   ; `
                              FDB   h_tor   ; {
                              FDB   h_or   ; |
                              FDB   h_fromr   ; }
                              FDB   h_not   ; ~
F0D0                          ENDIF      
F0D0                PTABEND:      
F0D0                             ; =============================================================================
F0D0                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F0D0                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F0D0                             ; =============================================================================
F0D0   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F0D2   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F0D4   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F0D6   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F0D8   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F0DA   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F0DC   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F0DE   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F0E0   39                     RTS      
F0E1   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F0E3   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F0E5   39                     RTS      
F0E6                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F0E6                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F0E6   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F0E8   37 06                  PULU   D   
F0EA   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F0EC   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F0EE                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )
F0EE   35 10        H_FROMR:   PULS   X   
F0F0   35 06                  PULS   D   
F0F2   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F0F4   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F0F6                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves up by n; TOS is the old pointer.
F0F6   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F0F8   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F0FA   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F0FC   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F0FE                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBCS   e_heap   ; a negative count wraps: too big
                              CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
                              LBHS   e_heap   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
F0FE                          ENDIF      
F0FE   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F100   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F102   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F104   39                     RTS      
F105                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
F105                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
F105                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS (39h) is
F105                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
F105                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
F105                             ; code is entered by JSR (the dispatcher's own), with the address already
F105                             ; popped: U points at the top data cell (big-endian, 2 bytes, stack grows
F105                             ; down) and the return address is on top of S. The code may pop and push
F105                             ; data cells by changing U; on return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F105                             ; keep Y (the interpreter's reading position), DP and S (balanced), and
F105                             ; return with RTS. A, B, X, CC may change.
F105   8D 98        H_GRAVE:   BSR   hexc   ; the digit after the grave, if any
F107   24 1A                  BCC   exec   
F109   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   
F10B   C6 10        HX1:      LDB   #16   
F10D   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F10E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   chkst   
F10E                          ENDIF      
F10E   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F110   8D 8D                  BSR   hexc   
F112   24 08                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F114   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F116   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F118   8D 85                  BSR   hexc   
F11A   25 EF                  BCS   hx1   
F11C                HX2:         
F11C                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   chkst   
F11C                          ENDIF      
F11C   86 39                  LDA   #39h   ; RTS
